Description:

CalDAV and JMAP scheduling no longer let a user schedule as another local
user's address.  Such an address is now ignored when it comes from the
user's calendar-user-address-set, from a Schedule-Address request header,
or from the addresses a stored calendar resource was scheduled with.
Before, a user could list another user's address and then update or cancel
that user's events in other local users' calendars, or reply in an
attendee's name.  Aliases that are no user's own address keep working; to
schedule on behalf of another user, share their calendar instead.


